==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-drown out.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{lb|en|idiom}} To [[cover]], [[obscure]], or [[overwhelm]] by being [[louder]] or more [[intense]] than.
#: {{syn|en|outdin}}
#: {{ux|en|He uses the music to '''drown out''' other noises around him.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2021|author=Michael Farris Smith|title=Nick|publisher=Little, Brown and Company|location=New York; Boston; London|chapter=27|page=142|passage=The fire had burned through the night and seemed barely affected by the efforts to '''drown''' it '''out''' and almost as if it were simply bored of the festival it had created, the fire lessened at daybreak.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Daniel Taylor|title=England and Wayne Rooney see off Scotland in their own back yard|work={{w|The Guardian}}|date=18 November 2014|url=http://www.theguardian.com/football/2014/nov/18/scotland-england-international-friendly-match-report|text=Charlie Mulgrew could easily have been shown two yellow cards by a stricter referee and amid all the usual Anglo-Scottish pleasantries, the two sets of fans put an awful lot of effort into trying to '''drown out''' one another’s national anthems.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|author={{w|Ava Max}}, {{w|Melanie Fontana}}, Michel Schulz, {{w|Ryan Tedder}}, {{w|Madison Love}}, and {{w|Cirkut}}|authorlabel=no|title={{w|Weapons (song)|Weapons}}|album={{w|Diamonds & Dancefloors}}|date=10 November 2022|artist=Ava Max|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pGnLEjFFBu8|text=Stop using your words as weapons / They're never gonna shoot me down / Stop, it's time that you learned a lesson / My love is gonna '''drown''' you '''out'''}}

